Link the CMakeDeps-provided GeoTIFF config target (plus libtiff) instead of module variables.

PDAL ships a FindGeoTIFF.cmake module that defines uppercase
GEOTIFF_INCLUDE_DIR/GEOTIFF_LIBRARY, but when Conan's CMakeDeps generates
a GeoTIFFConfig.cmake the CONFIG package wins and only the camel-case
variables plus the GeoTIFF::geotiff imported target exist. Use those so
headers and linking resolve under the Conan layout. libgeotiff's public
headers (xtiffio.h) include <tiffio.h> from libtiff, and the registry's
libgeotiff package does not aggregate libtiff's include dir into its own
package_info, so link libtiff::libtiff explicitly to propagate its
INTERFACE_INCLUDE_DIRECTORIES. Line numbers assume
0001-cmake-conan-rpath.patch (one line removed) is applied first.

diff --git a/CMakeLists.txt b/CMakeLists.txt
index 18ef599..a7e4683 100644
--- a/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -241,7 +241,7 @@ target_include_directories(${PDAL_LIB_NAME}
         ${PROJECT_BINARY_DIR}/include
         ${PDAL_VENDOR_DIR}
         ${NLOHMANN_INCLUDE_DIR}
-        ${GEOTIFF_INCLUDE_DIR}
+        ${GeoTIFF_INCLUDE_DIRS}
         ${UTFCPP_INCLUDE_DIR}
 )
 
@@ -251,7 +251,8 @@ target_link_libraries(${PDAL_LIB_NAME}
         ${CMAKE_DL_LIBS}
         GDAL::GDAL
         PROJ::proj
-        ${GEOTIFF_LIBRARY}
+        GeoTIFF::geotiff
+        libtiff::libtiff
         ${PDAL_REEXPORT}
         ${PDAL_ARBITER_LIB_NAME}
         ${PDAL_H3_LIB_NAME}
